            <ArticleTitle>Tl-201 scintigraphy in multivessel exercise-induced variant angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>675-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 53-year-old man presented for evaluation of nocturnal chest pain, consistent with angina pectoris. An exercise stress test reproduced his symptoms, however, exercise electrocardiograms were nondiagnostic. An exercise-thallium perfusion study confirmed vasospasm as the cause. This knowledge guided subsequent successful medical therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
